# Wave H.d.a — Collapse Denali wizard pure re-exports

## Problem

`apps/web/src/wizard/denali/` still holds **ten** files. Eight of them are one-line re-exports of `@app-tour/workspace-denali/host/*` — the hostile audit calls this a “fake decoupling” island (many paths, same coupling). Workspace-boundary **requires** product imports to stay inside `src/wizard/denali/` (P0-T-161 / P15-W-C2), so deleting the folder or spreading package imports into orchestration hooks would **regress** the thin-shell firewall.

## Decision (H.d.a — consolidate, do not dissolve)

1. Replace the eight pure re-export modules with a single intentional firewall module:
   - `apps/web/src/wizard/denali/adapters.tsx`
   - Re-exports: draft meta/identity, flat-edit chrome helpers, catalog prefetch context, localize validation message.
2. Keep non-trivial host glue separate:
   - `resolve-sync-workspace-plugin.ts` (draft-shell sync + registry async load — Wave B.a)
   - `workspace-plugin-id.ts` (constant alias used by sync resolve + shell)
3. Retarget all `./denali/<shim>` and `@/wizard/denali/<shim>` imports to `./denali/adapters` / `@/wizard/denali/adapters` (or the two glue modules).
4. Update `workspace-boundary` P15-W-C2 to assert:
   - `wizard/denali/adapters.tsx` exists and matches package host paths
   - pure per-symbol shim files are **absent**
   - folder still exists (firewall preserved)
5. Cap: `wizard/denali/` file count ≤ **3** after this tranche.

## Out of scope (H.d.b+)

- Deleting `wizard/denali/` entirely
- Absorbing draft/chrome symbols into more codegen bindings so adapters can shrink further
- Making create/flat orchestration import `@app-tour/workspace-denali` directly (would expand allowlist into shell)
- Confining remaining tours/exposure Denali imports into the firewall → [`wave-h-denali-import-firewall.mdoc`](./wave-h-denali-import-firewall.mdoc) (Wave H.h)

## Rationale

Audit debt is **path proliferation**, not the existence of a product-import firewall. One named `adapters.tsx` makes the remaining coupling honest and reviewable; sync resolve stays the only behavioral host entry.

## Verify

```bash
test $(find apps/web/src/wizard/denali -type f | wc -l) -le 3
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/workspace-boundary.spec.ts \
  test/denali-localize-validation-message.spec.ts \
  test/wave-h-denali-wizard-adapters.spec.ts \
  test/wizard-host-boundary.spec.ts
```
